  "question": {
    "text": "The voltage of the cell consisting of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Li</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mfenced></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced></math> electrodes is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5.92</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> at standard condition at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>298</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> . What is the voltage if the electrolyte consists of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi>LiF</mi></math> .<br />\r<br />\r<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.693</mo><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.314</mo><msup><mi>JK</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>and</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>96500</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math>"
  },
